# Gate 2 - Hand-Edited Generated Files

An agent edits `README.md`/`CLAUDE.md` (or any future generated `.md`)
directly because running the generator is one more tool call. The file
looks right and is no longer a render.

Finds every `.md` file anywhere in the repo carrying the
`livestage:generated` metadata block (Part 5.1) and asserts each one's
committed content still matches a fresh render of its declared source,
computed fresh by `check.cjs` every render. A new generated file joins this
contract automatically the moment it adopts the metadata block, no gate
update needed, unlike `readme:check`/`claude-md:check`/`examples:check`,
which only know about the specific files someone remembered to name.

